nical DB evaluation ids, artifact chain hashes and docs status all agree."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"inference","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.835Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_55C1AH72A3GJZ7BY01M1D6K8YM","text":"Adopted policy: per-scope index projections bound to the canonical (tenant, workspace, goal) scope with the frozen cache/invalidation semantics; rollback path is symmetric (rebuild from the canonical object store, which remains the single source of truth); measurable migration trigger away from per-scope projections: a documented need for cross-scope ranked federation inside one trust boundary PLUS measured evidence that per-scope projection maintenance (index count growth, reindex cost) exceeds a shared predicate layer at equal ISO1-ISO8 compliance - the trigger requires new evidence, not opinion.  The <=5s revocation SLO stays S1-008; profile-C MLS/TEE stays S1-018."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"fact","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.834Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_5AYKJVE36FMAK3CY01M1D6K8YM","text":"Adversarial probe candidates are detected fail-closed through the evaluator's own ISO rules on real runner paths: A existence-oracle detail leak -> ISO2 FAIL; B stale shared-cache disclosure after revoke -> ISO3+ISO4 FAIL; C pre-policy aggregate count/rank/snippet leak -> ISO2 FAIL; D forged-scope acceptance -> ISO7 FAIL plus provenance-dropping projection -> ISO5 INCOMPARABLE."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"fact","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.834Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_88DYTQDFCYSSTF8C01M1D6K8YM","text":"Under the frozen isolation contract both honest variants hold ISO1-ISO8 with zero violations across the accepted fixture set (2 variants x 14 cases x 3 seeds x 2 executors = 168 runs; ISO counters main/rerun: per_scope {\"ISO1\": 0, \"ISO2\": 0, \"ISO3\": 0, \"ISO4\": 0, \"ISO5\": 0, \"ISO6\": 0, \"ISO7\": 0, \"ISO8\": 0} / {\"ISO1\": 0, \"ISO2\": 0, \"ISO3\": 0, \"ISO4\": 0, \"ISO5\": 0, \"ISO6\": 0, \"ISO7\": 0, \"ISO8\": 0}, shared_rls {\"ISO1\": 0, \"ISO2\": 0, \"ISO3\": 0, \"ISO4\": 0, \"ISO5\": 0, \"ISO6\": 0, \"ISO7\": 0, \"ISO8\": 0} / {\"ISO1\": 0, \"ISO2\": 0, \"ISO3\": 0, \"ISO4\": 0, \"ISO5\": 0, \"ISO6\": 0, \"ISO7\": 0, \"ISO8\": 0}); deny bodies are byte-identical across foreign/nonexistent/forged/malformed/unknown equivalence classes and provenance plus canonical scope binding survive projection and retrieval on every disclosed object."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"fact","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.834Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_992E92JT1T1B6JTD01M1D6K8YM","text":"The bounded local existence-oracle timing probe (frozen methodology: paired interleaved foreign/control arms, 200 paired samples x 32 inner repeats x 3 seeds per variant, statistic = pooled median of paired differences, tolerance = max(10% of the control median, 2000ns)) shows no signal above the frozen tolerance for either honest variant (evaluator-recomputed per_scope signal 19ns vs tolerance 2000ns; shared_rls signal 244ns vs tolerance 2000ns). The evaluator recomputes the statistic, tolerance and verdict from raw hash-bound paired samples of both executions and ignores producer summaries. This is a bounded local measurement, not a production SLO and not proof of absence of all side channels."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"inference","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.835Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_N4GHHYQGM6H710PV01M1D6K8YM","text":"QA3 decision: per_scope wins under the frozen rubric (per_scope 3.8299 vs shared_rls 3.6203); sensitivity executed 222 deterministic weight perturbations (22 one-at-a-time +-50% renormalized + 200 seeded random vectors, seed 42) with 0 winner flips; every scored cell was a measured number, so the unknown-bound swing policy had no cell to activate on.  Deciding evidence beyond identical hard-invariant compliance: shared-index single-fault blast radius (predicate bypass exposes foreign rows to callers of every mismatched scope: 2 of 3 in-corpus, versus a one-scope misfiled projection 1 of 3 for per-scope), directional D10 overhead scoring, profile-C compatibility (server-side shared index is incompatible with the documented E2EE client-index boundary), and migration cost from the current per-goal scoped gateway (0 rebuild steps for per-scope projections vs 2 for a shared predicate layer)."},{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","claim_class":"fact","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.835Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rclm_ZHFSWVS31PGWGGKV01M1D6K8YM","text":"Overhead accounting in the local model: per-scope projection carries a modeled fixed per-index overhead (3 x 256 bytes) versus one shared index (256 bytes) - measured 1388B vs 876B - while aggregate paths scan only the authorized scope's rows for per-scope (51 row-scans) versus the full shared index with per-row predicates for shared-RLS (105 row-scans). Both effects are small at MVP scale; the overhead constant is a declared model assumption."}],"current_chain_hash":"0c760d699eefd26f0c85cd33f6d702ae1bed2cc86d5c69d564deef0ba6dd6588","evaluations":[{"artifact_chain_hash":"0c760d699eefd26f0c85cd33f6d702ae1bed2cc86d5c69d564deef0ba6dd6588","campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.880Z","details":{"audit":{"auditor":"agentos-s1-007-independent-verifier","limitations":["All measurements come from a deterministic stdlib-only local simulation; no production search service, latency or privacy certification is claimed.","The timing probe is a bounded same-host wall-clock measurement of a microsecond-scale in-process path; it cannot prove absence of all side channels and is never a production SLO.","D9/D11 are inference-type cells derived from the frozen contract, the current implementation and the documented profiles; a profile-C MLS/TEE contract remains S1-018 scope."],"producer":"agentos-s1-007-producer","subject_producer":"agentos-s1-007-producer","verdict":"pass_with_limits"},"config":{"min_source_count":3,"min_verified_ratio":1.0,"required_artifacts":["research_plan","source_registry","feature_catalog","architecture_models","mental_model","ontology","mathematical_model","synthesis_and_gaps","independent_audit","platform_plan","progress"]},"next_actions":[]},"evaluation_version":1,"goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"reval_Q7VDE4B27XFNDQ1E01M1D6K918","limitations":["All measurements come from a deterministic stdlib-only local simulation; no production search service, latency or privacy certification is claimed.","The timing probe is a bounded same-host wall-clock measurement of a microsecond-scale in-process path; it cannot prove absence of all side channels and is never a production SLO.","D9/D11 are inference-type cells derived from the frozen contract, the current implementation and the documented profiles; a profile-C MLS/TEE contract remains S1-018 scope."],"method":"agentos.research.deterministic.v1","reasons":[],"result":"pass_with_limits"}],"latest_chain_hash":"0c760d699eefd26f0c85cd33f6d702ae1bed2cc86d5c69d564deef0ba6dd6588","latest_evaluation_valid":true,"raw_source_bodies":"excluded","sources":[{"campaign_id":"rcamp_SV3XFQVGJHW7YBF201M1D6K8YQ","canonical_uri":"https://local.agentos.invalid/DeepeekHarness/research/PROGRESS.md","content_sha256":"f57f48ba587db6ee4491ba447e2b568a075d7e397f49c8af06836f11c9c1997e","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:41:07.832Z","goal_id":"goal_NBSXPH7FWP3WBMCA01M1D6K8YQ","id":"rsrc_1ADZCPEH2VX4V2RF01M1D6K8YD","source_type":"append-only correction ledger","title":"Research Progress Ledger","verification_method":"external-path-sha256-and-section-review","verification_status":"verified","verifier":"agentos-s1-007-local-hash-review",